{
  "0": "Across all four datasets, change only the tied normalized item-embedding radius multiplier from 0.75 to 0.775. The observed regressions at 0.70 and 0.80 motivate testing a smaller step near the incumbent, without assuming a monotonic response. Retain width 64, input/output tying, frequency modulation, topology, history, scoring, loss and optimizer. Use identical effective embedding weights during training and prediction.",
  "1": "Across all four datasets, replace forward ordinal position IDs with reverse ordinal IDs: the final nonpadding token receives position 1, its predecessor position 2, and padding remains 0. This may align positional representations across varying history lengths and give the appended prediction mask a consistent positional anchor. Preserve history truncation, bidirectional masked training, appended-mask readout, embedding parameterization, backbone, scoring, loss and optimizer; update inference consistently.",
  "2": "Across all four datasets, jointly lower learning rate from 7e-4 to 5e-4 and increase dropout from 0.1 to 0.15. Slower optimization coupled with stronger regularization may improve generalization; the regression at dropout 0.05 motivates exploring the opposite direction, without establishing its benefit. Keep dimensions, depth, heads, MAXLEN=128, batch size, Adam, loss and all representation/readout definitions fixed. Preserve seed 42, the 200-epoch cap and 200 batches per epoch.",
  "3": "Across all four datasets, replace each Transformer feed-forward sublayer with GEGLU: project the normalized state into two 2H-wide branches, multiply one branch by GELU of the other, then project back to H. Jointly learned gating may capture selective item-context interactions beyond the existing GELU feed-forward layer. Retain bidirectional attention, two blocks, residual placement, normalization, embeddings, sequence/readout, loss and optimizer. Train one model per category and load the same architecture in prediction."
}
